"An official Artonan invitation arrives as an image of a handwritten letter, translated by the System."
"It is followed by a teleport offer with no timer and no payment, unlike a summons."
"The letter wishes the guest welcome 'for a day or a year': our fires are warm, our bowls are full."
"Only a family member of age to offer the house's welcome may send one."
"In person, the host presents the letter with arms outstretched and the guest takes it in both hands."
"Some families mark their invitations by ink color; the art'h triplets' line uses brown ink."
